  data: {
    LLM: "Only bet the maximum when you have high cards in multiple suits. If you have an Ace in 3 suits, you have a very high probability of winning.\n\nCalculate the 'outs'. If you have only one suit (e.g., Spades) but it's the Ace, your chance of winning is roughly 1 in 4 (if a Spade is dealt, you win; if not, you lose). Betting the pot on a 25% chance is mathematically unsound.\n\nWatch the burn cards and previous players' turns. Card counting can slightly improve your odds by knowing which high cards have already been removed from the deck.",
